  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will learn that completing the square can be used to solve any quadratic equation, including equations that involve rational numbers that are not integers.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> Solve by completing the square when given a quadratic equation in which the coefficient of the squared term is 1. </item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 9.3.1: Solving Equations with Fractions </item>
  <item> 9.3.2: Using Completing the Square to Solve Equations </item>
  <list>
    <item> 9.3.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 9.3.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 9.3.3: Solve by Completing the Square </item>
  <list>
    <item> 9.3.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 9.3.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 9.3.4: Completing the Square with Fractions </item>
</list>
<para>After that, you'll <emphasis>practice and review</emphasis>.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent">
  <item> 9.3.5: Practice </item>
  <item> 9.3.6: Lesson Summary </item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
